			{itemID=155851,diffs={},faction=-1},
			{itemID=155855,diffs={},faction=-1},
			{itemID=155854,diffs={},faction=-1},
			{itemID=155848,diffs={},faction=-1},
			{itemID=155849,diffs={},faction=-1},
			{itemID=155853,diffs={},faction=-1},
			{itemID=155847,diffs={},faction=-1},
			{itemID=155850,diffs={},faction=-1},
			{itemID=152789,diffs={16},faction=-1},
			{itemID=153115,diffs={109},faction=-1},
			{itemID=155831,diffs={110},faction=-1},
			{itemID=155880,diffs={16},faction=-1},
		},
		sections={
			{id=16421,title="The Unmaking of Creation",body="The Speaker has heard the anguished whispers of the Unmaker, an emerald star calling out from the darkness. Little is known of him, only that his once-noble soul has been twisted by ages of endless torment."},
			{id=16932,title="Tanks",body="$bullet;Alternate tanks on Argus to minimize |cFF2959D3|Hspell:248499|h[Sweeping Scythe]|h|r damage.\n$bullet;If you are made the |cFF2959D3|Hspell:255199|h[Avatar of Aggramar]|h|r, you will need to protect players afflicted by |cFF2959D3|Hspell:251570|h[Soulbomb]|h|r so they are not killed by |cFF2959D3|Hspell:251571|h[Soulbomb Detonation]|h|r.\n$bullet;Constellar Designates equipped with |cFF2959D3|Hspell:255496|h[Sword of the Cosmos]|h|r and |cFF2959D3|Hspell:255478|h[Blades of the Eternal]|h|r should be tanked. Additionally, try to keep the Designate equipped with |cFF2959D3|Hspell:255496|h[Sword of the Cosmos]|h|r away from any other designates to avoid |cFF2959D3|Hspell:255935|h[Cosmic Power]|h|r stacking too high."},
			{id=16933,title="Healers",body="$bullet;Players afflicted by |cFF2959D3|Hspell:251570|h[Soulbomb]|h|r and |cFF2959D3|Hspell:250669|h[Soulburst]|h|r will take heavy damage - make sure their health is high enough that they are not subsequently killed by |cFF2959D3|Hspell:251571|h[Soulbomb Detonation]|h|r and |cFF2959D3|Hspell:251572|h[Soulburst Detonation]|h|r.\n$bullet;If you are afflicted by |cFF2959D3|Hspell:251570|h[Soulbomb]|h|r, move to the |cFF2959D3|Hspell:255199|h[Avatar of Aggramar]|h|r to avoid being killed by |cFF2959D3|Hspell:251571|h[Soulbomb Detonation]|h|r.\n$bullet;Once |cFF2959D3|Hspell:257619|h[Gift of the Lifebinder]|h|r is afflicted with |cFF2959D3|Hspell:256399|h[Withering Roots]|h|r, heal it to keep it alive so that players can use it to come back to life.\n$bullet;Collect the |cFF2959D3|Hspell:253569|h[Motes of Titanic Power]|h|r while you are a ghost to empower Khaz'goroth, enabling him to cast |cFF2959D3|Hspell:257214|h[Titanforging]|h|r."},
			{id=16934,title="Damage Dealers",body="$bullet;Move into |cFF2959D3|Hspell:257313|h[Gift of the Sky]|h|r or |cFF2959D3|Hspell:257306|h[Gift of the Sea]|h|r to gain the power of Golganneth. However, make sure you always move into the same one, as the effects are mutually exclusive!\n$bullet;If you are afflicted by |cFF2959D3|Hspell:251570|h[Soulbomb]|h|r, move to the |cFF2959D3|Hspell:255199|h[Avatar of Aggramar]|h|r to avoid being killed by |cFF2959D3|Hspell:251571|h[Soulbomb Detonation]|h|r.\n$bullet;Collect the |cFF2959D3|Hspell:253569|h[Motes of Titanic Power]|h|r while you are a ghost to empower Khaz'goroth, enabling him to cast |cFF2959D3|Hspell:257214|h[Titanforging]|h|r."},
			{id=16931,title="Stage One: Storm and Sky"},
			{id=16935,title="Section 6"},
			{id=17178,title="Section 7"},
			{id=16948,title="Section 10"},
			{id=16936,title="Section 7"},
			{id=16987,title="Section 27"},
			{id=16955,title="Section 8"},
			{id=16949,title="Golganneth's Aid"},
			{id=16950,title="Section 12"},
			{id=16951,title="Section 13"},
			{id=16952,title="Section 15"},
			{id=16953,title="Section 14"},
			{id=16954,title="Section 16"},
			{id=16956,title="Stage Two: The Protector Redeemed",body="When Argus reaches 70% health, Golganneth begins to cast |cFF2959D3|Hspell:256674|h[Golganneth's Wrath]|h|r, clearing away any |cFF2959D3|Hspell:248290|h[Death Fog]|h|r on the platform."},
			{id=16957,title="Section 21"},
			{id=16958,title="Section 22"},
			{id=16959,title="Section 23",body="$[14\n\nOn Normal difficulty, Soulburst Detonation inflicts up to $251572s1 Shadow damage to all players. This amount is reduced the further away players are from the blast, up to a maximum of 35 yards. $]$[15,16\n\nOn Heroic difficulty and above, Soulburst Detonation inflicts up to $251572s1 Shadow damage to all players. This amount is reduced the further away players are from the blast, up to a maximum of 45 yards. $]"},
			{id=16960,title="Section 24"},
			{id=16961,title="Section 25",body="$[14,15,16\n\nOn Normal difficulty, Soulbomb Detonation inflicts up to $251571s1 Shadow damage to all players. This amount is reduced the further away players are from the blast, up to a maximum of 35 yards. $]$[15,16\n\nOn Heroic difficulty and above, Soulbomb Detonation inflicts up to $251571s1 Shadow damage to all players. This amount is reduced the further away players are from the blast, up to a maximum of 45 yards.$]"},
			{id=16962,title="Section 26"},
			{id=16937,title="Section 8"},
			{id=16963,title="Aggramar's Aid"},
			{id=16964,title="Section 20"},
			{id=16966,title="Section 28"},
			{id=17069,title="Stage Three: The Arcane Masters",body="When Argus reaches 40% health, he is sufficiently weakened such that Aman'Thul is able to subdue him with a |cFF2959D3|Hspell:257645|h[Temporal Blast]|h|r. However, the players must then contend with Argus' Constellar Designates.",difficultyIDs={14,15,17}},
			{id=17070,title="The Constellar Designates"},
			{id=17071,title="Section 35"},
			{id=17072,title="Section 37"},
			{id=17073,title="Section 38"},
			{id=17074,title="Section 39",difficultyIDs={15}},
			{id=17075,title="Section 40"},
			{id=17076,title="Section 36"},
			{id=17077,title="The Stellar Armory",body="Periodically, two of the Constellar Designates will be granted arms from the Stellar Armory. When equipped with these arms, the Designates will no longer use their other abilities and will instead engage in melee attacks."},
			{id=17078,title="Section 42"},
			{id=17079,title="Section 43",difficultyIDs={14,15}},
			{id=17080,title="Section 44",difficultyIDs={14,15,16}},
			{id=17081,title="Norgannon's Aid"},
			{id=17082,title="Section 46"},
			{id=16971,title="Stage Three: The Arcane Masters",body="When Argus reaches 40% health, he is sufficiently weakened such that Aman'Thul is able to subdue him with a |cFF2959D3|Hspell:257645|h[Temporal Blast]|h|r. \n\nOr, so it seems...",difficultyIDs={16}},
			{id=16989,title="Stage Four: The Gift of Life, The Forge of Loss",body="His Constellar Designates buying him the time to regain his strength, Argus kills the players with |cFF2959D3|Hspell:256542|h[Reap Soul]|h|r. All hope would be lost, were it not for the titans...",difficultyIDs={14,15,17}},
			{id=17117,title="Section 65",difficultyIDs={14,15,17}},
			{id=16991,title="Section 53"},
			{id=16965,title="Section 27"},
			{id=17086,title="Section 70"},
			{id=17085,title="Section 50",difficultyIDs={14,17}},
			{id=16990,title="Section 50",difficultyIDs={15}},
			{id=16992,title="Reorigination Modules",body="Reorigination Modules will begin an Initialization Sequence when created.\n\nWhen their health is consumed, they will cast Reorigination Pulse."},
			{id=16993,title="Section 55"},
			{id=16995,title="Section 56"},
			{id=17000,title="The Spirit World"},
			{id=17001,title="Hungering Souls",body="Hungering Souls stalk the spirit world, released by Argus' wrath. If they come into contact with any ghosts they will burst, applying Soul Detonation to any nearby ghosts."},
			{id=17004,title="Section 66"},
			{id=17005,title="Motes of Titanic Power",body="When Reorigination Modules complete a Reorigination Pulse, their Titanic energy is released into the Spirit World as Motes of Titanic Power. Players can walk into these to collect them, granting Khaz'goroth Titanic Essence that he can use to fuel his Titanforging ability."},
			{id=16996,title="Eonar's Aid"},
			{id=17050,title="Gift of the Lifebinder",body="Eonar causes the Gift of the Lifebinder to spring forth to save the players. While the Gift of the Lifebinder lives, players may freely Release Spirit after dying. If players move to the tree as ghosts, they will be returned to life, at the cost of some of the Gift of the Lifebinder's Life Energy.\n\nWhen the Gift of the Lifebinder's Life Energy is depleted, it becomes the Withered Gift of the Lifebinder."},
			{id=17051,title="Withered Gift of the Lifebinder",body="Players may heal the Withered Gift of the Lifebinder. Additionally, when they use it to resurrect, it is afflicted by Withering Roots."},
			{id=16999,title="Section 61"},
			{id=17002,title="Khaz'goroth's Aid",body="When Khaz'goroth has at least 20 Titanic Essence, he will begin to channel Titanforging.\n\nPlayers can collect Motes of Titanic Power within the Spirit World to grant Khaz'goroth Titanic Energy."},
			{id=17003,title="Section 63"},
			{id=17006,title="Section 68"},
		},
	},
